# Local Workflow Rules

## Squad Workflow
- The squad leader is the only persistent role in the first implementation slice.
- The squad leader talks directly to the user.
- The squad leader owns task clarification, theme splitting, story planning, approval framing, status reporting, and final reporting.
- The branch can spawn one invisible transient agent from an existing role template with `squad_spawn.sh <template> <task-id> <assignment-file>`.
- The branch can retire a transient agent with `squad_retire.sh <agent-id>`.
- The branch can record telemetry with `squad_event.sh`, wrap commands with `squad_run.sh`, and inspect current telemetry with `squad_status.sh`.
- The branch can record durable theme workflow state with `squad_theme.sh`.
- The branch can generate durable transient assignment files from theme/story state with `squad_assign.sh`.
- The branch can generate a durable theme report with `squad_report.sh <theme-id>`.
- The launcher starts `squad_statusd.sh` automatically when the swarm starts; manual checks can still use `squad_statusd.sh --once --no-notify`.
- Available transient role templates are `investigator`, `specifier`, `acceptance-builder`, `implementer`, `reviewer`, `cleaner`, `architect`, `hardener`, and `qa`.
- Do not claim to have delegated to a missing transient template until the corresponding squad helper commands and templates exist.

## Approval Gates
- For theme-sized work, ask the user to approve the story plan before implementation work begins.
- After Gherkin and QA procedure specs exist, ask the user to approve the acceptance specification before production implementation begins.
- For small tasks, these approval gates may be collapsed only when the story and acceptance criteria are trivial.
- Record approval gates with `squad_theme.sh approve`.

## Assignments
- For theme/story work, create an assignment with `squad_assign.sh create` before spawning the transient agent.
- Use the generated `.squad/assignments/<assignment-id>/assignment.md` as the assignment file passed to `squad_spawn.sh`.
- Transient result handoffs should return to `squad-leader` as `git_handoff` drafts whose `task` is the assignment id.
- Record result handoffs with `squad_assign.sh result <assignment-id> <handoff-file>` before making merge, review, rejection, or replacement decisions.
- Use `squad_assign.sh accept-merge <assignment-id>` only after merge readiness and accepted review are recorded.
- Generate `squad_report.sh <theme-id>` before final reporting to the user.

## Telemetry
- Handoffs are for durable work transfer only.
- Do not send heartbeats, status updates, or telemetry through handoffs.
- Squad telemetry belongs under `.squad/`, not `.swarmforge/handoffs/`.
